<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan scraps 12.5 pct sales tax on cement.</title>
<headline>Pakistan scraps 12.5 pct sales tax on cement.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan scrapped a 12.5 percent sales tax on cement, but increased excise duty on the sector to 40 percent from 25 percent in the budget for fiscal 1997/98 (July-June).</p>
<p>&quot;Because of high tax rates, the cement production capacity is not being utilised properly,&quot; Finance Minister Sartaj Aziz said in his budget speech to parliament.</p>
<p>-- Islamabad newsroom 9251-274757</p>
